# Sasori – Claude-specific Rules

## Read First

| Topic | File |
|--------|------|
| CLI | `bin/index.ts` |
| HTTP API (multi-scan) | `src/api/createApiApp.ts`, `src/api/scanRegistry.ts`, `src/api/startApiServer.ts` |
| Crawl loop & Puppeteer | `src/crawler/crawler.ts` |
| Graph / queue / replay | `src/crawler/crawlStateManager.ts` |
| Vertices / edges | `src/crawler/crawlState.ts`, `src/crawler/crawlAction.ts` |
| Forms | `src/crawler/crawlInput.ts` |
| Selectors in page | `src/crawler/domPath.ts` |
| Browser launch | `src/browser/browser.ts` |
| Recorder login | `src/auth/authenticator.ts` |
| Config validation (CLI) | `src/models/configModel.ts` (`ConfigValidator`) |
| Types | `src/types/crawler.ts`, `src/types/input.ts` |

## Crawl Graph Mental Model

1. Root `CrawlState` after loading `entryPoint` and hashing DOM.
2. Each state exposes `CrawlAction[]` (clicks) and `CrawlInput[]` (fills).
3. Performing an action updates the page → new hash → either merge with existing state or create child state and link `parentAction` / `childState`.
4. Replay when the live page hash does not match the action’s parent: **`getOptimizedReplayPlan`** → `goto(baselineUrl)` then replay only post-baseline actions.

## Config

- Joi validation on startup: **`ConfigValidator`** from `configLoader` re-exports **`../models/configModel`** — that is the path **`start` uses**.
- There is also `src/config/configSchema.ts`; if both define the same keys, keep them in sync when editing.

## Puppeteer / Security Notes

- `stripDOM` and hashing run on **serialized HTML**; dynamic content order can affect hashes.
- `[click]` discovery uses **CDP** over all elements — very heavy on large pages.
- Scope: request interception + `inContext()` for navigation; `authInProgress` temporarily widens `includeRegexes` for the recorder.

## Types vs Code

- Do not assume `CrawlStateManagerInterface` in `types/crawler.ts` matches the class — implementation uses `rootState` + traversals, not `states: Map`.

## Tests

- Mirror paths: `tests/crawler/*` for crawler logic; run `npm test` after behavioral changes.
